@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF4FB
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #355777
hide footbox
autonumber
title Operator Generates N New Common Words into SQL

' Sources: backend/app/generate_common_words.py,
' backend/app/services/common_word_bank.py,
' backend/app/llm/{openrouter_common_bank,openrouter_common}.py,
' backend/app/schemas/common_word_bank.py.
actor Operator
participant "Backend CLI" as CLI
participant "Bank population service" as Service
participant "OpenRouter adapter" as Adapter
participant "OpenRouter LLM" as LLM
database "SQL / common_words" as DB

note over CLI, DB : Precondition: normal forward-only migration process applied through 0022.\nHistorical seed is removed; independently saved recall and operator content are retained.
Operator -> CLI : python -m app.generate_common_words --count N\nOptional --batch-size 1-20 (default 20)
opt Count omitted
  CLI --> Operator : Number of new Common words to generate?
  Operator -> CLI : Positive whole number N
end
CLI -> CLI : Validate count and batch size; load private backend settings
break Invalid input or configuration
  CLI --> Operator : Nonzero exit; safe diagnostic; no LLM generation
end
CLI -> Service : populate_bank(engine, N, settings, batch_size)
Service -> Service : saved=0; stalled=0
loop Until saved=N, failure, interruption, or stalled=3
  Service -> DB : Short read: SELECT all normalised_word values
  DB --> Service : Current exclusions
  Service -> DB : Close read connection / end transaction
  Service -> Adapter : generate_bank_words(min(batch_size, N-saved), exclusions)
  Adapter -> Adapter : Build content prompt and structured JSON schema
  Adapter -> LLM : Requested count + all existing words to exclude\nNo database transaction open during provider call
  note over Adapter, LLM : At most 3 HTTP attempts per call, within configured timeout.\nCapability fallback may remove schema enforcement or reasoning control once each.\nOther provider failures return to CLI without automatic operator retry.
  LLM --> Adapter : Word, part of speech, explanation, example, nullable IPA\nor provider error
  Adapter -> Adapter : Require completed bounded JSON; validate content fields\nReject empty, oversized, malformed or excess-count output
  break Provider or validation failure
    Adapter --> Service : Safe generation failure
    Service --> CLI : BankGenerationStopped(saved, N)
    CLI --> Operator : Exit 1; saved / remaining counts\nCompleted batches kept; retry with remaining --count
  end
  Adapter --> Service : Validated candidates
  Service -> Service : Validate batch; normalize words; skip existing/in-batch duplicates
  Service -> DB : BEGIN batch write
  loop Each new normalized candidate
    Service -> DB : INSERT with stable UUIDv5\nON CONFLICT (normalised_word) DO NOTHING RETURNING id
    DB --> Service : Inserted ID, or duplicate skipped
  end
  alt Database failure
    Service -> DB : ROLLBACK current batch
    Service --> CLI : Safe database error with prior saved count
    CLI --> Operator : Exit 1; completed batches kept; manual retry
    break Stop operator run
      note over CLI : Database credentials and provider bodies are not printed.
    end
  else Batch committed
    Service -> DB : COMMIT
    Service -> Service : Add actual inserted count to saved\nReset stalled on progress, otherwise increment
    Service --> CLI : progress(saved, N)
    CLI --> Operator : Saved X/N new Common words
  end
end
alt saved=N
  Service --> CLI : Return saved count
  CLI --> Operator : Exit 0; N new unique words saved
else Three consecutive batches added no words
  Service --> CLI : BankGenerationStopped(saved, N)
  CLI --> Operator : Exit 1; report remaining count for manual retry
end
CLI -> DB : Dispose engine in finally
note over Operator, DB : Operator interruption exits nonzero and preserves completed commits.\nCheck bank contents before choosing a new count after an interruption.\nThis command never creates learner questions, learning progress, or recall records.
@enduml
